The founder's find, from Giorgi's real account: he answered
„არ მცალია დამანებე თავი" on 6 October; the asker's assistant sent him
another question on the 7th and a reminder on the 9th.

Two causes. That line was not read as a decline, so it was stored as a
plain answer. And no decline ever stopped the next ask: declined_at was
recorded and nothing read it before sending again.

- Busy and „leave me alone" lines are typed declines (ka/en/ru/es):
  არ მცალია, დამანებე თავი, მომეშვი, ნუ მწერ, leave me alone, I'm busy,
  not interested, отстань, не пиши, déjame en paz, estoy ocupado/a. A line
  that carries something („…მაგრამ ხვალ დაგირეკავ") stays an answer.
- createAsk refuses any new question or follow-up from an asker to a person
  who declined that asker in the last 48 hours (reason declined_recently).
  The model is told to tell the owner calmly and move on. Only the owner
  naming the person again himself passes.
- The reminder sweep skips that person too.

The asker is still told once, by the decline path that already exists.

DONE WHEN: a helper answers „არ მცალია, დამანებე თავი" → 0 follow-ups and
0 reminders in 48h, and the asker is told once (2 of 2).

